2.
Definitions.
Page 1/5

The M.P. Madhyamik Shiksha Niyam, 1966
- In these rules, unless the context otherwise requires :-
(a)
"Act" means the Madhya Pradesh Madhyamik Shiksha Adhiniyam, 1965 (No. 23 of 1965);
(b)
"Dependent" means any of the relations of deceased/subscriber as defined in Rule 2(1) (iii) of the Madhya Pradesh
Contributory Provident Fund Rules;
(c)
"Interest" means the interest which is paid on a deposit in the Post Office Savings Bank, as may be determined from
time to time for deposits in the Post Office Savings Bank;
(d)
"Officer" means every whole-time salaried Officer, other than one whose services have been lent to the Board by the
Government;
(e)
"Salary" means monthly salary, and includes all fixed monthly allowances by way of pay, acting or personal allowance,
but does not include any other allowance;
(f)
"Savings Bank" means the Post Office Savings Bank;
(g)
"Section" means a section of the Act;
(h)
"State Service" means any service under the Government of Madhya Pradesh;
(i)
"Subscriber" means an officer on whose behalf a deposit is made under these Rules;
(j)
"Vice-Chairman" means the Vice-Chairman of the Board appointed under sub-section (1) of Section 16.
